{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cet7CckR3XvNibsyRPEUv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add a new error code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to the ErrorCode enum. This will be used when attempting to confirm a CANCELLED shipment.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new endpoint `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` that:\n   - Retrieves the shipment by ID (throws ResourceNotFoundException with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND if missing)\n   - If status is CREATED, update it to CONFIRMED and persist via repository.save()\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, do nothing (idempotent) and return the unchanged shipment\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE and HTTP 409\n   - Return ResponseEntity with HTTP 200 and the shipment body\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add five test cases:\n   - Test confirming a CREATED shipment transitions it to CONFIRMED\n   - Test confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment succeeds without change (idempotence)\n   - Test confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE error code\n   - Test confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error code\n   - Ensure error envelopes are properly structured (`.error.code` assertions)\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Creating a separate \"ConfirmRequest\" class — rejected because confirm needs no input parameters, so a simple POST to the resource endpoint is cleaner and follows REST conventions.\n- Using a separate service layer — rejected because the repository is already thin and the logic is simple (one status check and one update), and the existing codebase doesn't have a service layer for similar operations.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Process | Output | Mechanism |\n|------|-------|---------|--------|-----------|\n| CREATED→CONFIRMED | shipmentId | Load shipment, check status is CREATED, update to CONFIRMED, persist | HTTP 200 + Shipment JSON | repository.findById(), create new Shipment with CONFIRMED, repository.save(), return ResponseEntity |\n| Already CONFIRMED | shipmentId | Load shipment, check status is CONFIRMED, return unchanged | HTTP 200 + Shipment JSON | repository.findById(), return shipment unchanged via repository.save() |\n| CANCELLED | shipmentId | Load shipment, check status is CANCELLED | HTTP 409 + error envelope | throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE) → GlobalExceptionHandler catches it |\n| Not found | shipmentId | Try to load shipment | HTTP 404 + error envelope | repository.findById() returns null → throw ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND) → GlobalExceptionHandler catches it |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Test confirm creates→confirmed**: Create shipment with CREATED status, POST to confirm endpoint, assert 200 and status is now CONFIRMED\n2. **Test idempotence**: Create shipment, confirm once successfully, confirm again, assert 200 and no change to status or response\n3. **Test confirm cancelled fails**: Set up shipment directly in CANCELLED status, POST to confirm, assert 409 and error code is SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n4. **Test confirm missing fails**: POST to confirm with ID that doesn't exist, assert 404 and error code is SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n5. **Verify error envelopes**: All error cases assert both the HTTP status and the full error.code in the response body\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":411,"cache_read_input_tokens":19994,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":411},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"009d070d-cc2d-430b-ac0b-814f4d05a7f8","uuid":"574e4291-1498-4a3e-9a35-438a51fc4935","timestamp":"2026-09-09T15:32:48.692Z","request_id":"req_011Cet7Cc6EKYoADb4VZAH1W"}
