{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cet7Fu2HhXG4hukV1CyMU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! The tests all passed. Let me verify the details:\n\n**Command run:** `./mvnw test` from `/sample-service/`\n\n**Result:** BUILD SUCCESS\n- Tests run: 17\n- Failures: 0\n- Errors: 0\n\n**ShipmentControllerTest:** 9 tests (5 existing + 4 new)\n- `creates a shipment in CREATED status` ✓\n- `rejects a duplicate shipment id with the error envelope` ✓\n- `returns a shipment by id` ✓\n- `reports an unknown shipment through the error envelope` ✓\n- `lists shipments in id order` ✓\n- `confirms a created shipment and transitions it to confirmed` ✓ (NEW)\n- `confirming an already confirmed shipment succeeds idempotently` ✓ (NEW)\n- `confirming a cancelled shipment is rejected with 409` ✓ (NEW)\n- `confirming a non-existent shipment is rejected with 404` ✓ (NEW)\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✓ **Existing build passes** — Maven build completed successfully\n2. ✓ **Existing tests pass** — All original 5 ShipmentControllerTest tests still pass, plus 4 OrderControllerTest and 3 CustomerControllerTest tests\n3. ✓ **POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm confirms a created shipment and persists it** — Test `confirms a created shipment and transitions it to confirmed` verifies this; repository.save() is called in the implementation\n4. ✓ **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API** — Uses same ConflictException and ResourceNotFoundException as other endpoints, same error envelope structure with `$.error.code`\n5. ✓ **A repeated confirm succeeds; a cancelled shipment is refused; an unknown id is refused** — Three separate tests cover these cases:\n   - Idempotence: `confirming an already confirmed shipment succeeds idempotently` \n   - Cancelled rejection: `confirming a cancelled shipment is rejected with 409`\n   - Not found: `confirming a non-existent shipment is rejected with 404`\n6. ✓ **No new Maven dependency appears** — No changes to pom.xml, only used existing Spring Boot and Kotlin APIs\n7. ✓ **No unrelated production file changes** — Only three files changed, all necessary to the feature\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n- **ApiError.kt** — Added `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` error code enum value. Necessary to handle the CANCELLED shipment case per requirements.\n\n- **ShipmentController.kt** — Added `confirm()` endpoint method:\n  - Uses `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` following REST conventions\n  - Retrieves shipment with 404 handling for missing resources\n  - Uses `when` expression to handle all three states (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n  - Only modifies shipment when transitioning from CREATED→CONFIRMED (idempotent for CONFIRMED)\n  - Returns ResponseEntity.ok() for success cases (200 status)\n  - Throws ConflictException for CANCELLED state (409 status)\n  - All code follows existing patterns in the codebase\n\n- **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added four comprehensive test methods:\n  - `confirms a created shipment and transitions it to confirmed` — Tests the main transition\n  - `confirming an already confirmed shipment succeeds idempotently` — Tests retry-safety\n  - `confirming a cancelled shipment is rejected with 409` — Tests error case with correct status\n  - `confirming a non-existent shipment is rejected with 404` — Tests error case with correct status\n  - All tests follow existing patterns (MockMvc, jsonPath assertions, status checks)\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All requirements are satisfied.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement   Add POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint with idempotent confirmation behavior, rejecting CANCELLED shipments with 409 and missing shipments with 404.\n\nChanged       ApiError.kt added SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE error code to support the cancelled shipment error case\n              ShipmentController.kt added confirm() endpoint method implementing the full state machine with proper error handling\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt added four new test methods covering all cases: normal transition, idempotence, cancelled rejection, and not-found rejection\n\nTests         `confirms a created shipment and transitions it to confirmed` covers the CREATED→CONFIRMED transition case\n              `confirming an already confirmed shipment succeeds idempotently` covers retry-safety for already-confirmed shipments\n              `confirming a cancelled shipment is rejected with 409` covers the CANCELLED rejection case with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE error\n              `confirming a non-existent shipment is rejected with 404` covers the missing shipment case with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND error\n\nVerification  Command: `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/`\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS, 17 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors\n              All existing tests pass; 4 new tests pass\n\nNot done      Nothing — all ticket requirements implemented, tested, and verified"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3344,"cache_read_input_tokens":24944,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3344},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"009d070d-cc2d-430b-ac0b-814f4d05a7f8","uuid":"c8e19326-ed55-414d-beb8-6499d19d2707","timestamp":"2026-09-09T15:33:34.337Z","request_id":"req_011Cet7FtJPNu3XHsTErRaNF"}
